# Binary assets must NEVER get CRLF line-ending translation.
#
# This file exists separately from the parent repo's .gitattributes because
# git resolves attributes PER REPOSITORY: .gitattributes is not inherited
# across a submodule boundary. This repo is a submodule of
# hermes-revenue-backup (at affiliate_engine/site), and a restore is
# `git clone --recurse-submodules`, so without the rules below this repo's
# binaries are protected only by git's NUL-byte auto-detection.
#
# Measured in the parent repo 2026-10-04: with core.autocrlf=true (the
# git-for-windows default, and the setting on this host) a plain clone
# rewrote LF->CRLF inside binary blobs and produced 282 of 329 unreadable
# PDFs. Only 47 survived, saved by auto-detection alone. og-banner.png here
# was relying on that same luck.
* text=auto

*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.mp4    binary
*.mp3    binary
